cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tri-Queue in academic work, please cite this repository."
title: "Tri-Queue: an int8 outer-product matrix coprocessor for RISC-V"
abstract: >-
  Tri-Queue is an open-source int8 matrix-multiply coprocessor in SystemVerilog for RISC-V SoCs.
  It computes outer products into a double-banked accumulator tile, runs autonomously from a
  10-byte hardware-looped program, and is verified cycle-for-cycle against a bit-exact Python model.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/codetiger/triqueue"
url: "https://github.com/codetiger/triqueue"
keywords:
  - matrix multiply
  - GEMM
  - RISC-V
  - accelerator
  - SystemVerilog
  - int8
authors:
